{"abstract":[{"text":"A tool to decide whether there is sufficient evidence to reject a statistical hypothesis.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:7Science14HypothesisTestP","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HypothesisTest"}],"modules":[{"name":"Swift Science"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HypothesisTest"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HypothesisTest.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/lucca-mito\/swift-science\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Science\/Statistics\/Hypothesis%20Testing\/HypothesisTest.swift#L28"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","title":"HypothesisTest"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HypothesisTest"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"Definitions","level":2,"text":"Definitions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"statistical hypothesis","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is a constraint on a population parameter. For example, the parameter could be the population mean and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the constraint could be that it’s less than 10.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The statistical hypothesis being tested is always the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"null hypothesis","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". Informally, it represents the “status quo” hypothesis: nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interesting is going on, the current theory is correct, there are no new effects, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The null hypothesis is tested against an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"alternative hypothesis","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", which states that something interesting or unexpected is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"happening: the old theory needs to be updated, new previously-unseen effects are present, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can run a Wald test if the population parameter of interest to the hypothesis is the population mean (or any other parameter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"satisfying certain constraints; see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/WaldTest","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). To test whether the population mean equals 0:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["WaldTest(doesMeanEqual: 0).test(on: data)"],"copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","wrap":0}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/WaldTest"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Hypothesis-testing-fundamentals","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTestOutcome"],"title":"Hypothesis testing fundamentals"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Associated-Types","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/Sample"],"title":"Associated Types"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/criticalValue(at:for:)","doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/pValue(for:)","doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/test(on:atLevel:)","doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/testStatistic(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/science\/hypothesistest"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Science/documentation/Science":{"abstract":[{"text":"A scientific computing package for Swift.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science","images":[{"identifier":"swift-science-icon.png","type":"icon"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"text","text":"Swift Science"}],"role":"collection","title":"Swift Science","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/science"},"doc://Science/documentation/Science/HypothesisTest":{"abstract":[{"text":"A tool to decide whether there is sufficient evidence to reject a statistical hypothesis.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HypothesisTest"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HypothesisTest"}],"role":"symbol","title":"HypothesisTest","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/science\/hypothesistest"},"doc://Science/documentation/Science/HypothesisTest/Sample":{"abstract":[{"text":"The type used for sample data.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Sample"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Science\/documentation\/Science\/HypothesisTest\/Sample","kind":"symbol","required":true,"role":"symbol","title":"Sample","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/science\/hypothesistest\/sample"},"doc://Science/documentation/Science/HypothesisTest/criticalValue(at:for:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Calculates the critical value of the test.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"criticalValue"}